DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The Deny authentication service module for PAM, ppaamm__ddeennyy provides func‐
     tionality for all the PAM categories: authentication, account management,
     session management and password management.  In terms of the _m_o_d_u_l_e_-_t_y_p_e
     parameter, these are the “auth”, “account”, “session”, and “password”
     features.

     The Deny module will universally deny all requests.  It is primarily of
     use during testing, and to “null-out” unwanted functionality.

     The following options may be passed to the module:

     ddeebbuugg    syslog(3) debugging information at LOG_DEBUG level.

     nnoo__wwaarrnn  suppress warning messages to the user.  These messages include
              reasons why the user's authentication attempt was declined.

